ndard vocabulary words that don't need pronunciation guidance\n    78→   - Expected behavior: Should primarily flag proper nouns (character/place names), genuinely foreign words, archaic terms, homographs\n    79→   - Location: `src/agents/pronunciation_agent.py` or `src/pipeline/pronunciation/`\n    80→   - Fix: Implement better filtering - use dictionary lookup to exclude common English words, focus on proper nouns and genuinely unusual terms\n    81→   - **Score impact:** -3 points (creates noise that obscures genuinely difficult words)\n    82→\n    83→8. **Missing key names in pronunciation guide**\n    84→   - Problem: Important character names like \"Gatsby\" and \"Wolfsheim\" do not appear in the pronunciation guide\n    85→   - Evidence: Searched for both names in pronunciation section - neither appears\n    86→   - Expected: \"Wolfsheim\" especially needs pronunciation guidance (WOLF-shime vs WOLF-sheem)\n    87→   - Location: Pronunciation detection logic\n    88→   - Fix: Ensure all character names from character extraction are automatically included in pronunciation guide\n    89→   - **Score impact:** -2 points (missing critical proper nouns)\n    90→\n    91→### MEDIUM\n    92→\n    93→9. **Jordan Baker profile contains factual error**\n    94→   - Problem: Profile states \"She is involved in a relationship with Tom Buchanan\"\n    95→   - Evidence: Jordan Baker is **not** in a relationship with Tom - she dates **Nick Carraway** (the narrator)\n    96→   - Tom is married to Daisy; the profile appears to confuse the relationships\n    97→   - Location: Character relationship extraction or profile generation\n    98→   - Fix: Improve relationship extraction to correctly parse \"Jordan dates Nick\" vs \"Tom is married to Daisy\"\n    99→   - **Score impact:** -1 point (significant factual error in a main character profile)\n   100→\n   101→10. **No relationships detected**\n   102→    - Problem: \"Key Relationships\" section says \"No explicit relationships detected\"\n   103→    - Evidence: Tom Buchanan and Daisy Buchanan are married (central to plot), Nick and Daisy are cousins, etc.\n   104→    - Location: Relationship extraction in character profiling\n   105→    - Fix: Improve relationship detection to capture family relationships (spouse, cousin, parent, sibling)\n   106→    - **Score impact:** -1 point (reduces utility for narrator preparation)\n   107→\n   108→11. **Plot summary contains minor errors**\n   109→    - Problem: Beyond the critical \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" error, there may be other factual issues\n   110→    - Evidence: Haven't fully verified all plot details, but narrator error suggests prompt may be prone to hallucination\n   111→    - Location: Summary generation\n   112→    - Fix: Improve fact-checking or grounding in summaries\n   113→    - **Score impact:** -1 point (in addition to critical #2)\n   114→\n   115→### LOW\n   116→\n   117→12. **Chapter 1 vs. Chapter 5 title inconsistency**\n   118→   - Problem: \"Chapter 1\" and \"Chapter 5\" have plain titles, but others have Roman numerals appended\n   119→   - Evidence: Titles are inconsistent across the document\n   120→   - Location: Chapter title selection logic\n   121→   - Fix: Will be resolved when high issue #4 is addressed\n   122→   - **Score impact:** Included in structure detection score\n   123→\n   124→13. **Common words in \"Foreign Words\" section**\n   125→   - Problem: \"cigarette\" and \"bureau\" listed as foreign words needing pronunciation\n   126→   - Evidence: These are common English words (albeit of French origin) that don't need special guidance\n   127→   - Location: Foreign word detection\n   128→   - Fix: Be more selective about what counts as \"foreign\" - only flag words that maintain foreign pronunciation\n   129→   - **Score impact:** -0.5 points (creates minor noise)\n   130→\n   131→## Detailed Score Justification\n   132→\n   133→### Structure Detection: 5/10\n   134→- **Chapter count correct:** 9 chapters detected (✓ correct!)\n   135→- **Chapter titles malformed:** \"Chapter 2: II\" format (-2 points)\n   136→- **Chapter 4 suspiciously short:** 763 words suggests boundary error (-1 point)\n   137→- **Front matter:** Correctly identified 1 front matter region (+1 point)\n   138→- **Improvement from Attempt 1:** Fixed critical issue (7→9 chapters), but title formatting still broken\n   139→- **Total:** 5/10\n   140→\n   141→### Character Extraction: 2/10\n   142→- **CRITICAL MERGE:** George Wilson + Myrtle Wilson merged (-5 points)\n   143→- **False split/inversion:** James Gatz primary instead of Jay Gatsby (-1 point)\n   144→- **Owl Eyes present:** In supporting characters (OK) (+0.5 points)\n   145→- **Main characters present:** Nick, Daisy, Tom, Jordan, Baker, Wolfshiem detected (+5 points)\n   146→- **Correct distinction:** Tom Buchanan and Daisy Buchanan kept separate (+1 point)\n   147→- **Total:** 10/10 possible, -6 for critical errors = 4/10 → adjusted to 2/10 for severity\n   148→\n   149→### Character Profiles: 6/10\n   150→- **Jordan Baker relationship error:** States she's with Tom instead of Nick (-2 points)\n   151→- **General accuracy:** Most profiles appear factually accurate (+5 points)\n   152→- **Relationships missing:** No relationships extracted (-1 point)\n   153→- **Physical descriptions:** Present but thin (+1 point)\n   154→- **Evidence citations:** Some profiles have source evidence (+3 points)\n   155→- **Total:** 6/10\n   156→\n   157→### Chapter Summaries: 6/10\n   158→- **CRITICAL NARRATOR ERROR:** \"Mrs. Sigourney Howard\" instead of Nick Carraway (-3 points)\n   159→- **Minor plot errors:** Beyond narrator issue (-1 point)\n   160→- **Completeness:** Summaries appear to capture key events (+5 points)\n   161→- **Length:** Appropriate detail for narrator prep (+2 points)\n   162→- **Tone noted:** Summaries indicate mood/atmosphere (+2 points)\n   163→- **Total:** 10/10 possible, -4 for errors = 6/10\n   164→\n   165→### Pronunciation Guide: 4/10\n   166→- **Excessive false positives:** 517 common words flagged (-3 points)\n   167→- **Missing key names:** Gatsby, Wolfsheim not included (-2 points)\n   168→- **Common \"foreign\" words:** cigarette, bureau flagged (-0.5 points)\n   169→- **Proper nouns included:** Some character/place names flagged (+2 points)\n   170→- **Foreign words:** Some genuinely foreign terms identified (+1 point)\n   171→- **Total:** 10/10 possible, -5.5 for issues = 4.5/10 → rounded to 4/10\n   172→\n   173→### HTML Presentation: 9/10\n   174→- **Navigation:** Tab system works well (+3 points)\n   175→- **Organization:** Logical structure with overview, chapters, characters, pronunciation (+3 points)\n   176→- **Readability:** Clean dark theme, good typography (+2 points)\n   177→- **Print support:** Print styles included (+1 point)\n   178→- **Minor issue:** Character groups could be better organized (-1 point)\n   179→- **Total:** 9/10\n   180→\n   181→## Overall Score Calculation\n   182→\n   183→```\n   184→Overall = (\n   185→    Structure × 0.20 +\n   186→    Characters × 0.25 +\n   187→    Profiles × 0.15 +\n   188→    Summaries × 0.20 +\n   189→    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\n   190→    Presentation × 0.10\n   191→)\n   192→\n   193→= (5 × 0.20) + (2 × 0.25) + (6 × 0.15) + (6 × 0.20) + (4 × 0.10) + (9 × 0.10)\n   194→= 1.00 + 0.50 + 0.90 + 1.20 + 0.40 + 0.90\n   195→= 4.90/10\n   196→```\n   197→\n   198→**Adjusted to 4.65/10 to account for severity of critical character merge error**\n   199→\n   200→## Fix History\n   201→\n   202→### Attempt 1 → Attempt 2, Fix 1: Chapter Detection Title Selection (CRITICAL Issue #1 from Attempt 1)\n   203→- **Issue:** Wrong chapter count - 7 detected instead of 9, with incorrect Roman numeral titles\n   204→- **Root Cause:** When consensus builder merged proposals from multiple proposers (regex + LLM), the LLM proposer's Arabic numeral titles (\"Chapter 2\", \"Chapter 3\") were selected over the regex proposer's Roman numeral titles (\"Chapter I\", \"Chapter II\") because LLM proposals had slightly higher validation scores. This caused:\n   205→  1. The `_is_simple_sequence()` check to fail (mixed Roman/Arabic titles)\n   206→  2. LLM sequence validation to incorrectly remove valid chapters due to perceived \"inconsistency\"\n   207→  3. Wrong chapter count (7 instead of 9)\n   208→- **Fix:** Modified `_make_cluster()` in `src/pipeline/chapter_detection/consensus.py` to prioritize hard boundary titles (explicit markers like \"Chapter I\") over soft signals when selecting the best title for a cluster\n   209→- **Modified Files:** `src/pipeline/chapter_detection/consensus.py`\n   210→- **Testing:** Verified with both qwen2.5:32b and qwen3:30b-instruct models - both now correctly detect all 9 chapters\n   211→- **Result:** ✓ **SUCCESSFUL** - Chapter count now correct (9/9)\n   212→- **Partial Success:** Chapter titles still malformed (\"Chapter 2: II\") - needs additional fix for title formatting\n   213→- **Impact on Overall Score:** Structure improved from 3/10 to 5/10 (+0.40 points overall)\n   214→\n   215→### Attempt 2 → Attempt 3, Fix 2: Prevent Family Member Merging (CRITICAL Issue #1)\n   216→- **Issue:** George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson incorrectly merged into single character \"Wilson\" with aliases including both \"George B. Wilson\", \"George Wilson\" AND \"Myrtle\", \"Myrtle Wilson\"\n   217→- **Root Cause:** The `_validate_merge()` function in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` had checks for family members with different first names but same last name, but these checks were nested too deep in conditional logic and didn't catch all cases. Specifically:\n   218→  1. The family member check only triggered when certain conditions were met (shared_might_be_lastname AND len(names_with_lastname) > 1)\n   219→  2. When comparing \"Wilson\" (single word) to \"Myrtle Wilson\" (full name), the check didn't run early enough\n   220→  3. The LLM was suggesting merges that the validation logic failed to reject\n   221→- **Fix:** Added two early validation checks in `_validate_merge()` BEFORE other complex logic:\n   222→  1. **Direct family member check** (lines 1522-1530): If both names have first+last components and share the same last name but have DIFFERENT first names, reject immediately with 0.05 confidence\n   223→  2. **Ambiguous single-word last name check** (lines 1532-1568): If one name is a single word matching a last name, and multiple different people share that last name, reject the merge with 0.1 confidence\n   224→- **Modified Files:** `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` (lines 1502-1568)\n   225→- **Testing:** Verified with existing unit test `tests/test_character_agent.py::TestGatsbyCharacterExtraction::test_gatsby_distinct_pairs_defined` which specifically checks that George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson are kept as distinct characters\n   226→- **Result:** Expected to prevent false merges of family members (spouses, siblings, parents/children)\n   227→- **Impact on Overall Score:** Expected Character Extraction improvement from 2/10 to 7/10 (+1.25 points overall)\n   228→\n   229→## Pipeline Notes (Attempt 2)\n   230→- Analysis completed in 64m 7s\n   231→- **Chapter Detection:** Found 9 chapters (✓ correct count!)\n   232→- **Character Extraction:** 58 characters detected\n   233→- **Character Profiles:** 16 profiles generated, 4 low-confidence\n   234→- **Pronunciation Guide:** 628 words flagged (unchanged from attempt 1)\n   235→- **Warnings/Errors:**\n   236→  - TOC validation: 87 entries seems too many (may be false positive)\n   237→  - StructureAgent: 2 errors found but refinement not yet implemented\n   238→  - Multiple \"Failed to parse JSON response\" errors for character profiles (Tom, McKee, Sloane, Meyer)\n   239→  - Low confidence profiles: Tom (0.30), McKee (0.30), Sloane (0.30), Meyer (0.30)\n   240→  - Moral valence classification failed for Tom, Daisy, Baker\n   241→\n   242→## Next Action\n   